Q1. What are the primary goals of DevOps?

Interview Ready Answer

The primary goals of DevOps are to improve collaboration between
Development and Operations teams, automate software development and
deployment processes, deliver software faster, improve the reliability
and quality of software releases, and enable continuous monitoring and
feedback throughout the software development lifecycle.

Definition

Goals represent the objectives that DevOps aims to achieve.

Purpose

• Improve collaboration between teams.
• Automate repetitive manual tasks.
• Deliver software faster.
• Improve software quality and reliability.
• Reduce deployment failures.
• Enable continuous monitoring and feedback.
• Shorten the software release cycle.

Major Goals

• Collaboration
• Automation
• Faster Delivery
• Reliable Releases
• Continuous Monitoring
• Continuous Feedback

